<Placemark><name>#1 Kingston — North Kingston, Canbury / Park Rd (KT2 5/6)</name><styleUrl>#spot</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>#1</b> Kingston — North Kingston, Canbury / Park Rd (KT2 5/6)<br><b>Verdict:</b> Best long-term: strongest primary + comprehensive pair, a grammar on the doorstep with local priority, and the cheapest, flattest rents.<br><b>Primary:</b> St Luke's CofE (no faith test; 0.30–0.61 km), Latchmere (1.0 km) and Fern Hill (Outstanding; 2.2 km); St Paul's, St Agatha's and St Joseph's offered every applicant. Alexandra only within ~250 m.<br><b>Secondary:</b> The Kingston Academy — comprehensive, mixed; A8 64.6, P8 +1.16, Outstanding. Cut-off 1.20–1.30 km, so live within ~1 km of the Richmond Road entrance. Back-ups: Teddington School (comprehensive, mixed, A8 55.8; 5.1–5.8 km by road) and Coombe Girls' (comprehensive, girls, A8 57.2; Medium).<br><b>Grammar route:</b> Tiffin Girls' (grammar) is 1.1 km away and Canbury is in its Inner Area: up to 60 places for Inner Area girls ranked in the top 350.<br><b>Rent now:</b> £2247 pcm (2-bed flat) · travel £313.4 · total £2560.4<br><b>Main risk:</b> The Kingston Academy's margin is modest (0.9 vs 1.0 km comfort) and its measuring point moved in 2026. Kingston has no Tube; Waterloo trains take about 25–30 min.]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.296200,51.416600,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
