<Placemark><name>Emmanuel Church of England Primary School</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary (3-11, nursery) · Voluntary aided (CofE) · Ofsted Good · KS2 RWM 85% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest 0.204 km, widest 0.209 km (2024–26) · comfort radius 0.15 km<br>2023: 0.09 km · 2024: 0.21 km · 2025: 0.20 km · 2026: Oversubscribed – no distance published<br>Measured: straight line to the centre of the school<br>PAN 30 (2027-28 policy). 1) LAC/previously LAC and EHCP naming school; 2) children of permanent staff 2+ yrs; then 2/3 Route A: A1 siblings with church-member parent, A2 Emmanuel Church members, A3 recent movers attending Emmanuel, A4 members of another Christian church; 1/3 Route B: B1 siblings, B2 distance. Unfilled Route A places pass to Route B. Straight line from centre of home to central point of main building, 152-158 Mill Lane; lots as final tie-break. Nursery gives no stated priority. SIF for faith places.<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/100030">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|100030">results</a> · <a href="https://www.emmanuel.camden.sch.uk/attachments/download.asp?file=1032&amp;type=pdf">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.194549,51.551837,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>West Hampstead Primary School</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary (3-11, nursery) · Community · Ofsted Good · KS2 RWM 70% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest 2.82 km, widest 2.82 km (2024–26) · comfort radius 2.11 km<br>2023: 0.76 km · 2024: 2.82 km · 2025: Not oversubscribed – all applicants offered · 2026: No data<br>Measured: straight line to the centre of the school<br>PAN 60 (2027). Camden community criteria (2027-28): (a) looked-after/previously looked-after; (b) sibling on roll (only Reception-Y5 count; nursery pupils do not); (c) exceptional social/medical need for this school; (d) child of qualified teacher/TA at the school 2+ years or skill-shortage recruit; (e) distance, nearest first. Distance straight line ('as the crow flies') from home to centre of school by computerised mapping; distance is also the tie-breaker within b-d. Nursery attendance gives no priority.<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/100009">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|100009">results</a> · <a href="https://prod-web-assets.camden.gov.uk/documents/d/guest/camden-la-proposed-admission-arrangements-for-entry-in-sept-2027-28">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.199485,51.550672,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>St Luke's Church of England School</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary (4-11, no nursery) · Free school (CofE, single-academy trust) · Ofsted Good · KS2 RWM 97% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest 0.322 km, widest 0.924 km (2024–26) · comfort radius 0.24 km<br>2023: 0.63 km · 2024: 0.92 km · 2025: 0.32 km · 2026: No data<br>Measured: straight line to the centre of the school<br>PAN 15 (2027-28). a) LAC/previously LAC; b) siblings; c) exceptional social/medical need; d) child of qualified teacher 2+ yrs/skill shortage; e) distance. Policy describes distance both as home to 'centre of the school' and front door to 'main entrance' (inconsistent); random tie-break. School page: places determined by distance.<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/136807">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|136807">results</a> · <a href="https://www.stlukesschool.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/SLS-Admissions-Policy-2027-28.pdf">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.192832,51.557674,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Kingsgate Primary School</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary (3-11, nursery) · Community · Ofsted Outstanding · KS2 RWM 88% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest 1.419 km, widest 1.419 km (2024–26) · comfort radius 1.06 km<br>2023: Not oversubscribed – all applicants offered · 2024: 1.42 km · 2025: Not oversubscribed – all applicants offered · 2026: No data<br>Measured: straight line to the centre of the school<br>PAN 90 (2027). Camden community criteria (2027-28): (a) looked-after/previously looked-after; (b) sibling on roll (only Reception-Y5 count; nursery pupils do not); (c) exceptional social/medical need for this school; (d) child of qualified teacher/TA at the school 2+ years or skill-shortage recruit; (e) distance, nearest first. Distance straight line ('as the crow flies') from home to centre of school by computerised mapping; distance is also the tie-breaker within b-d. Nursery attendance gives no priority. Kingsgate uses a mid-way measuring point between Liddell Place and Kingsgate Road sites.<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/132245">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|132245">results</a> · <a href="https://prod-web-assets.camden.gov.uk/documents/d/guest/camden-la-proposed-admission-arrangements-for-entry-in-sept-2027-28">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.196741,51.543471,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>All Saints' CofE Primary School NW2</name><styleUrl>#pother</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary (4-11) · Voluntary aided (CofE) · Ofsted Good · KS2 RWM 57%<br>Cut-offs: tightest – km, widest – km (2024–26) · comfort radius nodata<br>2023: No data · 2024: No data · 2025: No data · 2026: No data<br>Measured: straight line<br>School site: PAN 30. Admissions policy not retrieved.<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/101315">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|101315">results</a> · <a href="https://www.allsaintsnw2.barnet.sch.uk/Information/Admissions/">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.199927,51.562126,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>St Eugene de Mazenod Roman Catholic Primary School</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary (4-11) · Voluntary aided (RC) · Ofsted Outstanding · KS2 RWM 82% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest 1.225 km, widest 1.225 km (2024–26) · comfort radius 0.92 km<br>2023: 1.47 km · 2024: 1.23 km · 2025: Not oversubscribed – all applicants offered · 2026: No data<br>Measured: straight line to the centre of the school<br>PAN 30. Own admission authority; policy 2027-28 published only as .docx, which could not be parsed. School welcomes all faiths and none but faith criteria apply.<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/100047">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|100047">results</a> · <a href="https://www.steugene.camden.sch.uk/attachments/download.asp?file=398&amp;type=docx">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.193725,51.540970,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Kilburn Grange School</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary (4-11) · Free school (Bellevue Place Education Trust) · Ofsted Good · KS2 RWM 66% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest – km, widest – km (2024–26) · comfort radius open<br>2023: No data · 2024: No data · 2025: Not oversubscribed – all applicants offered · 2026: No data<br>Measured: straight line, address point to address point<br>PAN 30. Own policy not retrieved; Brent tables show EHCP, Sibling, then Distance.<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/141751">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|141751">results</a> · <a href="https://www.brent.gov.uk/-/media/files/resident-documents/education-documents/how-places-were-offered-reception-2026.pdf?rev=730768d1ad084ee6beaed8f1d484b2a7&amp;hash=A9D804374A45256AABC636D15C1E2979">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.197057,51.540590,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Hampstead Parochial Church of England Primary School</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary (4-11) · Voluntary aided (CofE) · Ofsted Good · KS2 RWM 91% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest 0.314 km, widest 0.642 km (2024–26) · comfort radius 0.24 km<br>2023: 0.65 km · 2024: 0.64 km · 2025: 0.31 km · 2026: No data<br>Measured: straight line to the centre of the school<br>PAN 30. LAC first; then 50% Foundation (siblings + St John-at-Hampstead worship; siblings + other Christian church; St John worshippers; other Christian worshippers within 3 miles) and 50% Open (siblings; then nearest by Camden LA distance). Odd place goes to Foundation. Worship = twice a month for 2 years + clergy reference. Source: school admissions page (policy PDF not read).<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/100031">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|100031">results</a> · <a href="https://hampsteadprimary.co.uk/about-us/admissions/">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.179003,51.556444,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>St Mary's Kilburn Church of England Primary School</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary (3-11, nursery) · Voluntary aided (CofE) · Ofsted Outstanding · KS2 RWM 85% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest 0.235 km, widest 0.631 km (2024–26) · comfort radius 0.18 km<br>2023: 0.64 km · 2024: 0.23 km · 2025: 0.63 km · 2026: No data<br>Measured: straight line to the centre of the school<br>Max 30 (2027-28). 1) LAC/previously LAC; 2) St Mary's/St James's worshipper + sibling; 3) same, no sibling; 4) other Christian church + sibling; 5) other Christian church; 6) other siblings; 7) all others. Straight line centre of home to centre of school (Camden system); random tie-break. No staff criterion; nursery gives no priority.<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/100042">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|100042">results</a> · <a href="https://www.stmarykilburn.camden.sch.uk/attachments/download.asp?file=577&amp;type=pdf">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.193330,51.540370,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Christ Church CofE Primary School (Brondesbury)</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary (4-11) · Voluntary aided (CofE) · Ofsted Good · KS2 RWM 64% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest – km, widest – km (2024–26) · comfort radius open<br>2023: No data · 2024: No data · 2025: Not oversubscribed – all applicants offered · 2026: Not oversubscribed – all applicants offered<br>Measured: straight line, address point to address point<br>PAN 30. Policy not retrieved. Brent 2025 offer criteria: Sibling, Nursery, Other children living in parish, Any other applicants.<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/101533">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|101533">results</a> · <a href="https://www.brent.gov.uk/-/media/files/resident-documents/education-documents/how-places-were-offered-reception-2025.pdf?rev=3bed458d91924ab6b8bcd3d03c0e4137&amp;hash=6555BCF398B58933679C25B8600B368E">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.204081,51.540913,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>North West London Jewish Day School</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary (3-11, nursery) · Academy converter (Jewish) · Ofsted Good · KS2 RWM 81% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest 2.475 km, widest 4.088 km (2024–26) · comfort radius 1.86 km<br>2023: No data · 2024: No data · 2025: 2.48 km · 2026: 4.09 km<br>Measured: straight line, address point to address point<br>PAN 30. Policy not retrieved. Brent tables: EHCP, siblings, then religious-practice criteria; no place offered on a non-faith basis in 2025 or 2026.<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/141154">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|141154">results</a> · <a href="https://www.brent.gov.uk/-/media/files/resident-documents/education-documents/how-places-were-offered-reception-2026.pdf?rev=730768d1ad084ee6beaed8f1d484b2a7&amp;hash=A9D804374A45256AABC636D15C1E2979">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.212006,51.544766,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Childs Hill Primary School</name><styleUrl>#pother</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary (3-11, nursery) · Academy converter (The Elliot Foundation) · Ofsted Good · KS2 RWM 55%<br>Cut-offs: tightest – km, widest – km (2024–26) · comfort radius nodata<br>2023: No data · 2024: No data · 2025: No data · 2026: No data<br>Measured: straight line<br>PAN 60 (2027-28). EHCP; a) LAC/previously LAC; b) significant medical/social need; c) siblings; d) staff children 2+ yrs; e) nearest within catchment; f) nearest outside catchment. Straight line from home address point (OS) to school main gate; random tie-break. Nursery gives no priority.<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/147706">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|147706">results</a> · <a href="https://d180ur4pf89izg.cloudfront.net/uploads/asset/attachment/6471/Childs_Hill_Primary_School_Determined_Admissions_Policy_2027_28.pdf">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.206919,51.562269,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
