<Placemark><name>Fitzjohn's Primary School</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary (3-11, nursery) · Community · Ofsted Good · KS2 RWM 80% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest 0.66 km, widest 0.734 km (2024–26) · comfort radius 0.49 km<br>2023: 0.83 km · 2024: 0.73 km · 2025: 0.66 km · 2026: No data<br>Measured: straight line to the centre of the school<br>PAN 30 (2027). Camden community criteria (2027-28): (a) looked-after/previously looked-after; (b) sibling on roll (only Reception-Y5 count; nursery pupils do not); (c) exceptional social/medical need for this school; (d) child of qualified teacher/TA at the school 2+ years or skill-shortage recruit; (e) distance, nearest first. Distance straight line ('as the crow flies') from home to centre of school by computerised mapping; distance is also the tie-breaker within b-d. Nursery attendance gives no priority.<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/100026">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|100026">results</a> · <a href="https://prod-web-assets.camden.gov.uk/documents/d/guest/camden-la-proposed-admission-arrangements-for-entry-in-sept-2027-28">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.175836,51.553400,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>New End Primary School</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary (3-11, nursery) · Community · Ofsted Good · KS2 RWM 79% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest 1.085 km, widest 1.571 km (2024–26) · comfort radius 0.81 km<br>2023: Not oversubscribed – all applicants offered · 2024: 1.57 km · 2025: 1.08 km · 2026: No data<br>Measured: straight line to the centre of the school<br>PAN 30 (2027). Camden community criteria (2027-28): (a) looked-after/previously looked-after; (b) sibling on roll (only Reception-Y5 count; nursery pupils do not); (c) exceptional social/medical need for this school; (d) child of qualified teacher/TA at the school 2+ years or skill-shortage recruit; (e) distance, nearest first. Distance straight line ('as the crow flies') from home to centre of school by computerised mapping; distance is also the tie-breaker within b-d. Nursery attendance gives no priority.<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/100019">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|100019">results</a> · <a href="https://prod-web-assets.camden.gov.uk/documents/d/guest/camden-la-proposed-admission-arrangements-for-entry-in-sept-2027-28">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.176512,51.558140,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Christ Church Primary School, Hampstead</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary (4-11) · Voluntary aided (CofE) · Ofsted Outstanding · KS2 RWM 94% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest 0.529 km, widest 0.732 km (2024–26) · comfort radius 0.40 km<br>2023: 0.78 km · 2024: 0.73 km · 2025: 0.53 km · 2026: No data<br>Measured: straight line to the centre of the school<br>PAN 28 (Sept 2027). 1) LAC; 2) sibling + parent worships at Christ Church; 3) sibling; 4) parent worships at Christ Church; 5) lives within one mile; 6) parent worships at another Christian church; 7) all others. Straight line home to centre of school (LA GIS); random draw if equal.<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/100028">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|100028">results</a> · <a href="https://christchurchschool.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Christ-Church-NW3-Admissions-Criteria-September-2027.pdf">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.176597,51.559257,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Islamia Primary School</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary (4-11) · Voluntary aided (Muslim) · Ofsted Good · KS2 RWM 76% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest 2.008 km, widest 2.616 km (2024–26) · comfort radius 1.51 km<br>2023: No data · 2024: No data · 2025: 2.01 km · 2026: 2.62 km<br>Measured: straight line, address point to address point<br>PAN 60. Policy not retrieved. Brent tables: children of staff; Muslim children of converts; of alumni; Muslim siblings; Muslim religious practice.<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/101574">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|101574">results</a> · <a href="https://www.brent.gov.uk/-/media/files/resident-documents/education-documents/how-places-were-offered-reception-2026.pdf?rev=730768d1ad084ee6beaed8f1d484b2a7&amp;hash=A9D804374A45256AABC636D15C1E2979">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.207939,51.539614,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Anson Primary School</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary (3-11, nursery) · Community · Ofsted Good · KS2 RWM 63% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest 1.018 km, widest 1.018 km (2024–26) · comfort radius 0.76 km<br>2023: No data · 2024: No data · 2025: 1.02 km · 2026: 5.18 km<br>Measured: straight line, address point to address point<br>PAN 52 (56 from 2027). Brent community criteria (determined 2025-26): EHCP first; then looked-after/previously looked-after; medical/social need; children of staff (2+ yrs or skill shortage); siblings; all others. Within each, straight-line distance from home address point to school address point (LLPG); random tie-break. 2027-28 text not retrieved.<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/101495">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|101495">results</a> · <a href="https://www.brent.gov.uk/media/16421246/determined-brent-community-school-admissions-arrangements-for-2025-to-2026.pdf">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.219899,51.553879,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
