<Placemark><name>Smallwood Primary School and Language Unit</name><styleUrl>#pother</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary · Community school · Ofsted Good · KS2 RWM 40%<br>Cut-offs: tightest 0.355 km, widest 0.684 km (2024–26) · comfort radius 0.27 km<br>2023: Not oversubscribed – all applicants offered · 2024: 0.35 km · 2025: 0.47 km · 2026: 0.68 km<br>Measured: straight line to the centre of the site<br>Wandsworth community schools without priority areas 2026-27: EHCP first; 1 LAC/PLA; 2 exceptional medical/social; 3 sibling on roll; 4 staff children (2+ yrs or shortage, 0.6 FTE, max 1 per form of entry); 5 straight-line distance, Wandsworth GIS from property to central point of school site. No nursery priority. Ties: random. (2027-28 document not found.)<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/101021">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|101021">results</a> · <a href="https://www.wandsworth.gov.uk/media/syljlpnm/community_schools_without_priority_areas_admission_policy_2026_27.pdf">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.178074,51.431215,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Barnes Primary School</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary (3-11, nursery) · Community school · Ofsted Outstanding · KS2 RWM 94% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest 0.557 km, widest 0.557 km (2024–26) · comfort radius 0.42 km<br>2023: 0.24 km · 2024: No data · 2025: No data · 2026: 0.56 km<br>Measured: shortest walking route (road/footpath) for community schools; straight line at Deer Park, St Elizabeth's, Thomson House <b>(walking route)</b><br>Richmond community arrangements 2027/28: EHCP first; (i) looked after/previously looked after; (ii) exceptional family, social or medical need; (iii) staff children (2+ yrs); (iv) siblings; (v) nearest by shortest road/footpath route (GIS) to nearest pedestrian gate; ties by distance then lots. No catchment; nursery gives no priority.<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/102902">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|102902">results</a> · <a href="https://www.marshgate.richmond.sch.uk/attachments/documents.asp?id=930">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.250185,51.469444,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>St Osmund's Catholic Primary School</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary (4-11) · Academy converter (Catholic) · Ofsted Good · KS2 RWM 80% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest – km, widest – km (2024–26) · comfort radius nodata<br>2023: No data · 2024: No data · 2025: No data · 2026: No data<br>Measured: shortest walking route (road/footpath) for community schools; straight line at Deer Park, St Elizabeth's, Thomson House <b>(walking route)</b><br>2027/28, PAN 30: 1 baptised Catholic LAC/PLAC; 2 baptised Catholic with sibling; 3 other baptised Catholic; 4 other LAC/PLAC; 5 other siblings; 6 Eastern Christian; 7 other Christian/other faiths (evidence); 8 others. Within 2-8: exceptional need, then shortest road/footpath route to pedestrian gate (Richmond GIS); lots for ties. SIF required for faith categories.<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/149926">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|102919">results</a> · <a href="https://www.st-osmunds.richmond.sch.uk/admissions/">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.245306,51.474272,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
