<Placemark><name>Lowther Primary School</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary (3-11, nursery) · Community school · Ofsted Good · KS2 RWM 80% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest – km, widest – km (2024–26) · comfort radius open<br>2023: Not oversubscribed – all applicants offered · 2024: No data · 2025: No data · 2026: Not oversubscribed – all applicants offered<br>Measured: shortest walking route (road/footpath) for community schools; straight line at Deer Park, St Elizabeth's, Thomson House <b>(walking route)</b><br>Richmond community arrangements 2027/28: EHCP first; (i) looked after/previously looked after; (ii) exceptional family, social or medical need; (iii) staff children (2+ yrs); (iv) siblings; (v) nearest by shortest road/footpath route (GIS) to nearest pedestrian gate; ties by distance then lots. No catchment; nursery gives no priority.<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/102892">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|102892">results</a> · <a href="https://www.marshgate.richmond.sch.uk/attachments/documents.asp?id=930">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.239697,51.483469,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>St Mary Magdalen's Catholic Primary School</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary (4-11) · Voluntary aided school (Catholic) · Ofsted Good · KS2 RWM 76% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest – km, widest – km (2024–26) · comfort radius open<br>2023: No data · 2024: No data · 2025: No data · 2026: Not oversubscribed – all applicants offered<br>Measured: shortest walking route (road/footpath) for community schools; straight line at Deer Park, St Elizabeth's, Thomson House <b>(walking route)</b><br>2027 brochure, PAN 30: 1 Catholic LAC/PLAC; 2 baptised Catholic with Certificate of Practice; 3 other baptised Catholic; 4 other LAC/PLAC; 5 catechumens; 6 Eastern Orthodox; 7 other faiths/denominations; 8 others. Within each: sibling, then social/pastoral/medical need, then shortest route (GIS); lots. (2026/27 policy instead: Catholic LAC; Catholic siblings; other Catholics; other LAC; other siblings; other Christians/faiths; others.)<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/102909">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|102909">results</a> · <a href="https://www.st-marymagdalens.richmond.sch.uk/admissions/">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.261204,51.468592,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Sheen Mount Primary School</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary · Community school · Ofsted Good · KS2 RWM 82% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest – km, widest – km (2024–26) · comfort radius open<br>2023: 1.15 km · 2024: No data · 2025: No data · 2026: Not oversubscribed – all applicants offered<br>Measured: shortest walking route (road/footpath) for community schools; straight line at Deer Park, St Elizabeth's, Thomson House <b>(walking route)</b><br>Richmond community arrangements 2027/28: EHCP first; (i) looked after/previously looked after; (ii) exceptional family, social or medical need; (iii) staff children (2+ yrs); (iv) siblings (incl. paired junior); (v) nearest by shortest road/footpath route (GIS, address point to named pedestrian gate); ties by distance then lots. No catchment; nursery attendance gives no priority. Note 2023 AfC table had sibling as (iii), staff as (iv).<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/102897">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|102897">results</a> · <a href="https://www.richmond.gov.uk/media/wqskgp2n/how_primary_places_were_offered.pdf">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.275596,51.461097,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
