<Placemark><name>The Vineyard Primary School</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary · Community school · Ofsted Good · KS2 RWM 86% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest 1.672 km, widest 1.672 km (2024–26) · comfort radius 1.25 km<br>2023: Not oversubscribed – all applicants offered · 2024: No data · 2025: No data · 2026: 1.67 km<br>Measured: shortest walking route (road/footpath) for community schools; straight line at Deer Park, St Elizabeth's, Thomson House <b>(walking route)</b><br>Richmond community arrangements 2027/28: EHCP first; (i) looked after/previously looked after; (ii) exceptional family, social or medical need; (iii) staff children (2+ yrs); (iv) siblings (incl. paired junior); (v) nearest by shortest road/footpath route (GIS, address point to named pedestrian gate); ties by distance then lots. No catchment; nursery attendance gives no priority. Note 2023 AfC table had sibling as (iii), staff as (iv).<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/102906">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|102906">results</a> · <a href="https://www.richmond.gov.uk/media/wqskgp2n/how_primary_places_were_offered.pdf">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.298464,51.454291,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
