<Placemark><name>St Joseph's Catholic Primary</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary (with nursery) · Academy (converted 2025; Roman Catholic) · Ofsted Good · KS2 RWM 62% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest – km, widest – km (2024–26) · comfort radius open<br>2023: No data · 2024: No data · 2025: No data · 2026: Not oversubscribed – all applicants offered<br>Measured: straight line to the nearest pedestrian gate<br>2027 brochure summary: 1 LAC/PLAC Catholic; 2 baptised Catholic; 3 other LAC/PLAC; 4 catechumens; 5 Eastern Orthodox; 6 other Christian; 7 siblings; 8 other faiths; 9 no religion. Within each: siblings, staff children, exceptional need, then distance; lots final. 2024 brochure version also tiered by Mass attendance and parish (St Raphael). PAN 30.<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/149924">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|102596">results</a> · <a href="https://www.stlukes.kingston.sch.uk/_site/data/files/3-admissions/reception/C4C8762B69A69F1AB3984D8D708A65E9.pdf">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.294968,51.408685,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>St John's CofE Primary</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary (with nursery, ages 3-11) · Voluntary aided · Ofsted Good · KS2 RWM 72% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest 0.329 km, widest 0.624 km (2024–26) · comfort radius 0.25 km<br>2023: 0.27 km · 2024: 0.33 km · 2025: 0.62 km · 2026: Not oversubscribed – all applicants offered<br>Measured: straight line to the nearest pedestrian gate<br>2027 brochure summary: 1 LAC; 2 exceptional medical/social need; 3 siblings; 4 worshipping members of named Kingston churches; 5 worshipping members of other Christian churches in designated area; 6 nearest by straight line to main gate; tie-break distance. No staff criterion. Brochure text still references 2022; full policy (Google Drive) not readable.<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/102589">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|102589">results</a> · <a href="https://www.stlukes.kingston.sch.uk/_site/data/files/3-admissions/reception/C4C8762B69A69F1AB3984D8D708A65E9.pdf">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.299607,51.404166,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>King Athelstan Primary</name><styleUrl>#pother</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary (with nursery, ages 2-11) · Community · Ofsted Good · KS2 RWM 59%<br>Cut-offs: tightest – km, widest – km (2024–26) · comfort radius open<br>2023: 0.78 km · 2024: Not oversubscribed – all applicants offered · 2025: Not oversubscribed – all applicants offered · 2026: Not oversubscribed – all applicants offered<br>Measured: straight line to the nearest pedestrian gate<br>Kingston community 2027/28: EHCP named; 1 LAC/previously LAC; 2 siblings (same school or paired junior); 3 exceptional family/social/medical need; 4 children of staff (2+ yrs or skill-shortage post); 5 distance. Straight line (GIS, OS address point) to nearest pedestrian gate used by year group; tie-break distance then lots. Nursery attendance gives no priority. PAN 60.<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/102579">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|102579">results</a> · <a href="https://moderngov.kingston.gov.uk//documents/s112516/Annex%201_%20Admissions%20arrangements%20for%20community.pdf">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.295038,51.405251,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>St Luke's CofE Primary</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary (with nursery, ages 3-11) · Foundation (CofE) · Ofsted Good · KS2 RWM 78% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest 0.298 km, widest 0.606 km (2024–26) · comfort radius 0.22 km<br>2023: 0.46 km · 2024: 0.30 km · 2025: 0.61 km · 2026: 0.52 km<br>Measured: straight line to the nearest pedestrian gate<br>2027 policy: 1 LAC/PLAC; 2 exceptional medical/social need; 3 sibling at school; 4 nearest by straight line (Kingston GIS) to Elm Road or Acre Road gate; tie-break distance then lots. No faith or staff criterion; nursery gives no priority. PAN 30.<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/102604">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|102604">results</a> · <a href="https://www.stlukes.kingston.sch.uk/_site/data/files/3-admissions/reception/29A73BECAC1274BE569840638FB27E15.pdf">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.296283,51.416240,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Hampton Wick Infant and Nursery</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Infant (with nursery, ages 3-7) · Community (Richmond) · Ofsted Outstanding · KS2 RWM 62% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest – km, widest – km (2024–26) · comfort radius nodata<br>2023: Not oversubscribed – all applicants offered · 2024: No data · 2025: No data · 2026: No data<br>Measured: shortest walking route (road/footpath) for community schools; straight line at Deer Park, St Elizabeth's, Thomson House <b>(walking route)</b><br>Richmond community (2025 brochure): 1 LAC/PLAC; 2 exceptional need; 3 siblings at same address (same school or paired junior); 4 staff children (2+ yrs); 5 nearest. Distance = shortest route by road/maintained footpath to nearest pedestrian gate (GIS), not straight line; tie-break lots. Junior no longer gives Year 2 priority (criterion ended 31 Aug 2024).<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/102889">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|102911">results</a> · <a href="https://www.bishopperrin.richmond.sch.uk/ckfinder/userfiles/files/Richmond_s_infant__junior__primary_and_secondary_schools_brochure__2025.pdf">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.311149,51.418316,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
