<Placemark><name>Latchmere Primary</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary (with nursery, ages 3-11) · Academy (Latchmere Academy Trust) · Ofsted Good · KS2 RWM 79% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest 1.003 km, widest 1.003 km (2024–26) · comfort radius 0.75 km<br>2023: Not oversubscribed – all applicants offered · 2024: 1.00 km · 2025: Not oversubscribed – all applicants offered · 2026: Not oversubscribed – all applicants offered<br>Measured: straight line to the nearest pedestrian gate<br>2027 brochure: 1 LAC/PLAC; 2 siblings (incl. step/half/foster); 3 exceptional family/social/medical need; 4 staff children (2+ yrs); 5 nearest by straight line to nearest gate; distance then lots. PAN 90.<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/138689">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|138689">results</a> · <a href="https://www.stlukes.kingston.sch.uk/_site/data/files/3-admissions/reception/C4C8762B69A69F1AB3984D8D708A65E9.pdf">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.296294,51.422139,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Maple Infant</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Infant (with nursery) · Community · Ofsted Good · KS2 RWM 76% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest 1.01 km, widest 1.38 km (2024–26) · comfort radius 0.76 km<br>2023: 3.02 km · 2024: 1.38 km · 2025: 1.01 km · 2026: 8.44 km<br>Measured: straight line to the nearest pedestrian gate<br>Kingston community 2027/28: EHCP named; 1 LAC/previously LAC; 2 siblings (same school or paired junior); 3 exceptional family/social/medical need; 4 children of staff (2+ yrs or skill-shortage post); 5 distance. Straight line (GIS, OS address point) to nearest pedestrian gate used by year group; tie-break distance then lots. Nursery attendance gives no priority. PAN 90. Not a "paired" school in the community arrangements, so siblings at the junior do not count. Junior gives Maple Year 2 pupils within 1 mile priority (open places criterion 5 of 6).<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/102577">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|102588">results</a> · <a href="https://moderngov.kingston.gov.uk//documents/s112516/Annex%201_%20Admissions%20arrangements%20for%20community.pdf">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.306904,51.394991,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>St Agatha's Catholic Primary</name><styleUrl>#pgood</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Primary (with nursery, ages 3-11) · Academy (Roman Catholic) · Ofsted Good · KS2 RWM 70% · <b>good primary</b><br>Cut-offs: tightest – km, widest – km (2024–26) · comfort radius open<br>2023: Not oversubscribed – all applicants offered · 2024: Not oversubscribed – all applicants offered · 2025: Not oversubscribed – all applicants offered · 2026: Not oversubscribed – all applicants offered<br>Measured: straight line to the nearest pedestrian gate<br>2027 brochure: 1 LAC/PLAC Catholic; 2 baptised Catholic; 3 other LAC/PLAC; 4 catechumens; 5 other Christian; 6 other faiths; 7 others. Within category: sibling, staff parent or exceptional need raises priority, then distance. Brochure PAN 60; LA tables show 30 places.<br>Sources: <a href="https://reports.ofsted.gov.uk/provider/21/137856">ofsted</a> · <a href="https://api.education.gov.uk/statistics/v1/data-sets/019afee4-e5d0-72f9-9a8f-d7a1a56eac1d/query?indicators=IwjBz,i2s6X,ODwCL&amp;filters.in=EXcPq&amp;locations.in=SCH|urn|137856">results</a> · <a href="https://www.stlukes.kingston.sch.uk/_site/data/files/3-admissions/reception/C4C8762B69A69F1AB3984D8D708A65E9.pdf">admissions</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.293123,51.421931,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
