<Folder><name>Off-lead parks</name>
<Placemark><name>Canbury Gardens</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[North Kingston<br>Off lead: Off lead allowed (no PSPO in Kingston); keep out of fenced playground; riverside path shared with cyclists<br>Thames-side linear park between Kingston Bridge and Teddington Lock; small for a daily run but links to Thames Path. Kingston confirmed in April 2025 it has no PSPOs in place (dog or otherwise).<br>Royal Borough of Kingston upon Thames · <a href="https://moderngov.kingston.gov.uk/documents/s109279/Annex%201%20-%20Council%20Questions%20and%20Responses%20-%201%20April%202025.pdf">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.307500,51.417500,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Richmond Park</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[North Kingston; St Margarets/East Twickenham; Mortlake/East Sheen & Barnes<br>Off lead: Off lead allowed away from deer; MANDATORY on lead everywhere 1 May-31 July (deer birthing); advised on lead/avoid deer Sept-Nov (rut); on lead around ponds and in skylark zones (Lawn Field, Crown Field, The Bog); on lead in Isabella Plantation; no dogs in Pembroke Lodge Gardens or playgrounds<br>Chasing deer is an offence. Royal Parks rule of thumb max 4 dogs per person; commercial walkers need licence. Gates: Kingston Gate (North Kingston), Richmond Gate/Petersham (St Margarets side), Sheen Gate/Bog Gate/Roehampton Gate (East Sheen/Barnes).<br>The Royal Parks · <a href="https://royalparks.org.uk/visit/parks/richmond-park/faqs ; https://www.royalparks.org.uk/deer-safety-advice">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.273300,51.442500,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Bushy Park</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[North Kingston<br>Off lead: Off lead allowed away from deer; MANDATORY on lead everywhere 1 May-31 July (deer birthing); keep on lead near deer / avoid Sept-Nov (rut); on short lead in skylark zones Mar-Sept (south of Oval Plantation, west of Hampton Wick cricket ground); on lead around rivers and ponds; no dogs in Woodland Gardens<br>Reached from North Kingston via Kingston Bridge / Hampton Wick (c.1 km). Royal Parks rule of thumb max 4 dogs per person.<br>The Royal Parks · <a href="https://royalparks.org.uk/visit/parks/bushy-park/faqs ; https://royalparks.org.uk/press-release/dogs-leads-be-compulsory-during-deer-birthing-season">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.339400,51.411900,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Home Park (Hampton Court Park)</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[North Kingston<br>Off lead: NOT suitable for off-lead: HRP asks that dogs are kept on a lead at all times; stay 50 m from deer and keep to mown paths (deer park)<br>750-acre deer park behind Hampton Court Palace, open 07:00-20:00. Dogs chasing deer have killed deer; prosecution threatened. Good on-lead walk only.<br>Historic Royal Palaces · <a href="https://www.hrp.org.uk/hampton-court-palace/whats-on/home-park-and-the-long-water/">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.323000,51.403000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Marble Hill Park</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[St Margarets/East Twickenham<br>Off lead: Off lead allowed in most of the park under close supervision; on lead in and around the cafe; fenced children's play area is dog-free<br>65-66 acres riverside parkland; English Heritage site (not council). Proposed code of conduct: professional walkers max 4 dogs, £250 licence.<br>English Heritage · <a href="https://www.english-heritage.org.uk/visit/places/marble-hill/plan-your-visit/facilities/">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.313900,51.448600,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Moormead and Bandy Recreation Ground</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[St Margarets/East Twickenham<br>Off lead: Off lead allowed (not in Richmond PSPO on-lead schedule); dogs excluded from fenced playground and enclosed sports/tennis areas; max 4 dogs<br>Local rec with football pitches, tennis, playground, River Crane along west side. Moor Mead Road TW1 1JS.<br>London Borough of Richmond upon Thames · <a href="https://www.richmond.gov.uk/services/parks_and_open_spaces/find_a_park/moormead_and_bandy_recreation_ground ; https://richmond.gov.uk/media/16037/pspo_dog_control_order.pdf">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.326500,51.455500,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Orleans Gardens</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[St Margarets/East Twickenham<br>Off lead: Small riverside garden; council page says there is a grassy area where dogs are not allowed; playground dog-free; otherwise general Richmond PSPO applies<br>Too small for a daily run; mainly a riverside link between Marble Hill and Twickenham riverside. Orleans Road TW1 3BJ.<br>London Borough of Richmond upon Thames · <a href="https://www.richmond.gov.uk/services/parks_and_open_spaces/find_a_park/orleans_gardens">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.318500,51.446500,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Wimbledon Common (incl. Putney Heath)</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Wimbledon SW19<br>Off lead: Off lead allowed ('run free') if in sight and under effective control; on lead around all ponds and on The Plain (mown paths only) during bird nesting season 1 Mar-31 Aug; follow notices; requested max 4 dogs per group<br>Independent statutory body (Conservators), not Merton council; byelaws apply. Golf course on common land - move off fairways. Over 75 dog bins.<br>Wimbledon and Putney Commons Conservators · <a href="https://www.wpcc.org.uk/activities/dogs">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.233000,51.435000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Wimbledon Park</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Wimbledon SW19<br>Off lead: Off lead allowed (Merton has no dog-control PSPO in force as of Nov 2026); keep out of play areas, splash pad, sports facilities and the lake; a Merton PSPO with dog measures is under consultation (closes 2 Nov 2026)<br>27 ha public park with large lake, athletics track, tennis, bowling green; adjoining former golf course is AELTC land, not public park.<br>London Borough of Merton (idverde contractor) · <a href="https://www.merton.gov.uk/wimbledon-park ; https://Merton.gov.uk/communities-and-neighbourhoods/dog-control-orders">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.206000,51.436000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Dundonald Recreation Ground</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Wimbledon SW19<br>Off lead: Off lead allowed (no Merton PSPO in force); keep out of playground and sports areas<br>Small local rec behind Dundonald Primary; mainly for quick walks. Merton proposed PSPO measures not yet in force.<br>London Borough of Merton · <a href="https://Merton.gov.uk/communities-and-neighbourhoods/dog-control-orders">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.213000,51.417500,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Morden Hall Park</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Wimbledon SW19<br>Off lead: Off lead allowed across most of the estate if recall is reliable; on lead in the Rose Garden, around buildings (Stableyard, Snuff Mill, cafes, garden centre), the adventure play area and the wetland boardwalk<br>National Trust 3-pawprint site, 125 acres, River Wandle; six dog bins. c.3 km from Wimbledon town centre.<br>National Trust · <a href="https://nationaltrust.org.uk/visit/london/morden-hall-park/visiting-morden-hall-park-with-your-dog">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.190000,51.402800,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Barnes Common</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Mortlake/East Sheen & Barnes<br>Off lead: Off lead allowed under control (may mean leading up when asked); Richmond PSPO: on lead at Barnes Pond, max 4 dogs, dogs excluded from enclosed play/sports areas<br>Local Nature Reserve (acid grassland, woodland), cricket and football pitch; Vine Road SW13 0NE. Managed by charity Barnes Common Ltd on behalf of the council.<br>Barnes Common Ltd (for LB Richmond upon Thames) · <a href="https://richmond.gov.uk/services/parks_and_open_spaces/find_a_park/barnes_common ; https://richmond.gov.uk/media/16037/pspo_dog_control_order.pdf">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.241900,51.464400,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Sheen Common / East Sheen Common</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Mortlake/East Sheen & Barnes<br>Off lead: Off lead allowed in the woodland (popular with dog walkers); Richmond PSPO requires lead at Sheen Common Pond; dogs excluded from bowling green, tennis courts and natural playground; max 4 dogs<br>Woodland adjoining Richmond Park at Bog Gate (links straight into the park). Freehold National Trust, managed by Richmond council. Fife Road SW14 7EL.<br>LB Richmond upon Thames (freehold National Trust) · <a href="https://www.richmond.gov.uk/services/parks_and_open_spaces/find_a_park/sheen_common ; https://richmond.gov.uk/media/16037/pspo_dog_control_order.pdf">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.271500,51.455500,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Palewell Common and Fields</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Mortlake/East Sheen & Barnes<br>Off lead: Off lead allowed on the open fields (not in PSPO on-lead schedule); dogs excluded from play areas, paddling pool and enclosed sports areas; keep off pitch-and-putt course; max 4 dogs<br>Pitch & putt, petanque, cricket, football, cafe. Enmore Gardens SW14 8RF. Connects to Richmond Park via Palewell gate path.<br>London Borough of Richmond upon Thames · <a href="https://www.richmond.gov.uk/services/parks_and_open_spaces/find_a_park/palewell_common_and_fields ; https://richmond.gov.uk/media/16037/pspo_dog_control_order.pdf">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.256500,51.461500,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Barn Elms / WWT London Wetland Centre</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Mortlake/East Sheen & Barnes<br>Off lead: NOT a dog venue: Richmond PSPO bans dogs from Barn Elms playing fields at all times; WWT London Wetland Centre admits assistance dogs only. Thames towpath alongside is on-lead (highway) under the PSPO<br>Included so the map does not suggest it as a dog walk. Use Barnes Common or Putney Lower Common instead.<br>LB Richmond upon Thames (playing fields) / WWT (wetland centre) · <a href="https://richmond.gov.uk/media/16037/pspo_dog_control_order.pdf ; https://www.wwt.org.uk/wetland-centres/london/plan-your-visit/">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.237000,51.476000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Clapham Common</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Clapham/Battersea<br>Off lead: Off lead allowed on the open common; dog-free: Eagle Pond, Mount Pond, Bandstand Beds, play areas (Battersea Rise, Windmill Drive), skate park/sports hub, The Spinney, fenced sports facilities; on lead at the four cafe seating areas; proposed Lambeth limit max 4 dogs with max 2 off lead<br>Lambeth's Dog Control PSPO text is from the 2023 draft; adoption status could not be confirmed online on 2026-11-01. A fenced Westside dog exercise area exists.<br>London Borough of Lambeth · <a href="https://www.lambeth.gov.uk/sites/default/files/2023-01/Draft%20Dog%20Control%20PSPO.pdf ; https://www.lambeth.gov.uk/consultations/have-your-say-dog-control-lambeth">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.150000,51.461100,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Wandsworth Common</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Clapham/Battersea<br>Off lead: Off lead allowed on the open common; on lead near the lake/ponds (dogs must not enter water), north of the tennis courts and around Skylark cafe; excluded from all playgrounds and the cricket field; max 4 dogs (6 with licence); lead by direction of Parks Police<br>Wandsworth Parks & Open Spaces PSPO in force since Oct 2025 (renewed borough dog controls). Exact on-lead/exclusion boundaries are on council maps (wandsworth_pspo_maps.pdf).<br>London Borough of Wandsworth · <a href="https://www.wandsworthcommon.org/dogs ; https://www.wandsworth.gov.uk/community-safety/antisocial-behaviour/public-spaces-protection-order/">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.173600,51.449400,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Battersea Park</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Clapham/Battersea<br>Off lead: Off lead allowed on open grass; dogs excluded from certain areas (children's play areas, sports facilities, lake and water features, formal gardens as mapped); on lead in car parks, cafe seating and by direction; max 4 dogs<br>Council lists Battersea Park as a park where dogs are excluded from certain areas only (not whole park). Exact zones on the council PSPO map.<br>London Borough of Wandsworth · <a href="https://www.wandsworth.gov.uk/business-and-licensing/licensing/animal-welfare-licensing/dog-walking-licence/dog-free-parks ; https://wandsworth.gov.uk/media/otjb0422/wandsworth_pspo_maps.pdf">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.156400,51.479200,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Hampstead Heath</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[West Hampstead<br>Off lead: Off lead allowed across the open Heath if the dog responds to recall; on lead in formal landscapes (Golders Hill Park), sports pitches and where signed; excluded from playgrounds, fenced conservation areas and ponds (except designated dog-swimming spots); max 4 dogs per person; professionals need licence<br>City of London byelaws 21-23 apply. Not Camden council land. Around 1.5-2 km from West Hampstead.<br>City of London Corporation · <a href="https://www.cityoflondon.gov.uk/things-to-do/green-spaces/hampstead-heath/activities-at-hampstead-heath/dog-walking-at-hampstead-heath ; https://democracy.cityoflondon.gov.uk/documents/s143326/Appendix%201%20Hampstead%20Heath%20Dog%20Walking%20Code%20of%20Conduct.pdf">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.162800,51.560800,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Fortune Green</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[West Hampstead<br>Off lead: Small green; Camden PSPO lists Fortune Green among long-standing dog-free areas (press report says the picnic area); adjacent Hampstead Cemetery is on-lead only<br>Not a daily off-lead option; Camden general rule elsewhere: off lead in parks except gated playgrounds/sports areas, on lead on streets.<br>London Borough of Camden · <a href="https://www.camden.gov.uk/pspo-dog-control-mess ; https://www.camdennewjournal.co.uk/article/dogs-to-get-asbod-from-parts-of-parks">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.197500,51.554700,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Kilburn Grange Park</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[West Hampstead<br>Off lead: Off lead allowed under Camden's general rule (parks and green spaces) except gated playgrounds and gated sports areas; on lead if asked by an officer<br>Small neighbourhood park with large playground and sports facilities; not named in Camden's exclusion list.<br>London Borough of Camden · <a href="https://www.camden.gov.uk/pspo-dog-control-mess">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.196500,51.544500,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Epsom Common Local Nature Reserve</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Epsom & Ewell<br>Off lead: Off lead allowed under close control; council advises lead near sheep and recall/unclip if cattle approach (seasonal cattle grazing in fenced compartments); keep out of ponds; advised max 6 dogs<br>SSSI/LNR adjoining Ashtead Common (City of London). Stew Ponds car park off Christ Church Road. No borough dog PSPO found.<br>Epsom & Ewell Borough Council (Countryside Team) · <a href="https://www.epsom-ewell.gov.uk/sites/default/files/documents/residents/venues-sport-and-leisure-facilities/parks/local-nature-reserves/Epsom%20Common%20Local%20nature%20reserve%20information%202019.pdf ; https://epsom-ewell.gov.uk/residents/access-nature/accessing-nature-responsibly/enjoying-countryside-your-dog">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.290000,51.333000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Epsom Downs</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Epsom & Ewell<br>Off lead: On lead until 12 noon while racehorses train (Conservators' request); free to run off lead after noon; keep under control near horses; racecourse closed on race days<br>Epsom & Walton Downs c.600 acres of chalk downland managed by the Conservators (council + Jockey Club). Commercial dog walking licensing considered 2024.<br>Epsom and Walton Downs Conservators · <a href="https://www.thejockeyclub.co.uk/epsom/about/dog-walking">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.252000,51.313000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Horton Country Park Local Nature Reserve</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Epsom & Ewell<br>Off lead: Off lead allowed under close control; keep out of winter woodland-works areas; fouling an offence<br>400 acres of woodland and grassland, car park off Horton Lane. Also hosts Hobbledown farm (separate, no dogs).<br>Epsom & Ewell Borough Council · <a href="https://www.epsom-ewell.gov.uk/sites/default/files/documents/residents/venues-sport-and-leisure-facilities/parks/local-nature-reserves/Horton%20Country%20Park%20Local%20Nature%20Reserve%20information%202019.pdf">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.289000,51.348000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Nonsuch Park</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Epsom & Ewell<br>Off lead: Off lead allowed in open parkland (code says 'safe, designated areas'); on lead near Nonsuch Pantry cafe and front of Mansion; dogs excluded from the Formal Garden and the picnic areas at Cheam, Sparrow Farm Road and London Road gates; private walkers advised max 4, licensed commercial max 6<br>300 acres on the Epsom & Ewell / Sutton border; commercial dog-walking licence scheme adopted 2024-25.<br>Nonsuch Park Joint Management Committee (Epsom & Ewell BC and LB Sutton) · <a href="https://democracy.epsom-ewell.gov.uk/documents/s34405/Nonsuch%20Park%20Commercial%20Dog-Walking%20Licensing%20Policy%20Dog-Walking%20Code%20of%20Conduct%20Appendix%201.pdf">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.229000,51.358000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Alexandra Recreation Ground</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Epsom & Ewell<br>Off lead: Off lead allowed (no borough dog PSPO found); keep out of playground, skate park and sports pitches; fouling £80 FPN<br>Town rec off Alexandra Road KT17; rules inferred from council general dog guidance, no park-specific page found.<br>Epsom & Ewell Borough Council · <a href="https://epsom-ewell.gov.uk/residents/access-nature/accessing-nature-responsibly/enjoying-countryside-your-dog">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.254500,51.334500,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Rosebery Park</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Epsom & Ewell<br>Off lead: Off lead allowed under control (no borough dog PSPO found); keep out of playground and away from the pond<br>Small formal town park near Epsom station; rules inferred from council general guidance, no park-specific page found.<br>Epsom & Ewell Borough Council · <a href="https://epsom-ewell.gov.uk/residents/access-nature/accessing-nature-responsibly/enjoying-countryside-your-dog">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.269000,51.330000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Verulamium Park</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[St Albans<br>Off lead: Off lead allowed (St Albans has no dog PSPOs); keep out of playgrounds and the lake; cattle graze Seabrook Meadow seasonally; 10+ dog bins<br>66.9 ha incl. lake and Roman remains. Council says it has no PSPOs applying to dogs; a street-drinking PSPO covers the park.<br>St Albans City & District Council (John O'Conner contractor) · <a href="https://www.stalbans.gov.uk/sites/default/files/attachments/Verulamium%20Park%20GAP%202024-29%20Draft%20v4.pdf ; https://www.stalbans.gov.uk/pests-and-animal-welfare">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.356000,51.750000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Clarence Park</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[St Albans<br>Off lead: Off lead allowed (no dog PSPO in district); keep out of playground, cricket ground and sports facilities<br>Victorian park by St Albans City station; no park-specific dog page found.<br>St Albans City & District Council · <a href="https://www.stalbans.gov.uk/pests-and-animal-welfare">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.323100,51.755600,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Heartwood Forest</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[St Albans<br>Off lead: Dogs welcome; Woodland Trust standard guidance: off lead if under control, on lead near livestock and in bird-nesting season where signed, pick up<br>346.7 ha new native forest north of Sandridge (grid TL162114), c.4-5 km from St Albans centre.<br>Woodland Trust · <a href="https://www.woodlandtrust.org.uk/visiting-woods/woods/heartwood-forest">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.313000,51.782000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Bernards Heath</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[St Albans<br>Off lead: Off lead allowed (no dog PSPO in district); keep out of playground and playing pitches<br>Open heath/recreation ground north of the city centre; no park-specific dog page found.<br>St Albans City & District Council · <a href="https://www.stalbans.gov.uk/pests-and-animal-welfare">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.335000,51.763900,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Highfield Park</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[St Albans<br>Off lead: Off lead allowed under control (charity park, no PSPO); keep out of playgrounds and orchard events areas<br>c.60-acre rural park on former hospital land, run by Highfield Park Trust since 1996; trust site has no dog page.<br>Highfield Park Trust (charity) · <a href="https://www.highfieldparktrust.co.uk/">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.313500,51.739500,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Jersey Farm Woodland Park</name><styleUrl>#park</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[St Albans<br>Off lead: Off lead allowed (no dog PSPO in district); under control near grazing/wildflower meadows<br>Community woodland/meadow between Jersey Farm estate and Sandridge; no park-specific dog page found.<br>St Albans City & District Council · <a href="https://www.stalbans.gov.uk/pests-and-animal-welfare">source</a> (2026-11-01)]]></description><Point><coordinates>-0.321500,51.774500,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
